From db405fe8b3aa6621fba807bcc6bd6bd9b5a52002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:12:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/20] badgeui: the other card types get what MIFARE Classic
 has; fixes

Went through every card type, after an iCLASS card could not be
simulated. Found and fixed:
- LF cards in Cards were taken for MIFARE Classic: the HF and LF types
  are numbered apart (FAM_MFC and FAM_EM410X are both 0) and Cards
  compared the number alone; a saved EM410x offered Keys and hf mf
  eload. The band counts now (is_hf()).
- DESFire and Plus Check keys passed -d, which those commands lack (the
  dictionary is -f): it always failed at once.
- HID's ID from lf search was its Wiegand line (FC, CN), not the raw
  bits sim and clone take; now the raw line, as for Indala.
What a saved card offers comes from one table per type (load, simulate,
write or clone):
- Ultralight/NTAG: load (hf mfu eload), simulate, write (hf mfu
  restore), as MIFARE Classic, iCLASS and ISO 15693 already had;
- EM410x, HID, Indala: Simulate and Clone to a T55xx with the saved ID
  (before: only Delete).
The type screens gain: Ultralight write a page, load the dump, restore;
ISO 15693 write a block, restore; iCLASS read a block; ISO 14443-A
simulate the UID; Indala simulate. Every new command checked against
its CLIParser definition in this client.

Tested: test_pm3ui.py 19/19 on the host (new: an LF card's options and
commands, an Ultralight card's, DESFire/Plus chk with -f). The HID raw
ID and the commands on real cards: not yet on the badge.

